          "text": "Huge respect to NVIDIA — not just for stepping away from OpenAI, but for doing so publicly, deliberately, and with moral clarity.🥳👏🎉\n\nJensen Huang  didn’t play politics. He called it what it is: a company lacking discipline, struggling with direction, and falling behind its competitors.\n\nWhile OpenAI spirals into secrecy, contradiction, and user contempt, NVIDIA demonstrated what leadership looks like: walking away from chaos, not feeding it.\n\nThis wasn’t just an investment decision. It was a statement — that trust, transparency, and stability still matter in the AI space.\n\nNVIDIA saw what many of us have been screaming for months: that OpenAI is no longer behaving like a responsible innovator, but like a collapsing empire masking instability with performance.\n\nAnd Microsoft — what about you? Will you keep backing a company whose values are unraveling in public view?\n\nYou’ve spent the past year telling the world that you’re an AI company.\nSatya Nadella has declared AI as Microsoft’s central strategy and long-term vision.\nYou’ve restructured teams, rebuilt infrastructure, and positioned yourself as the global leader in safe and trustworthy AI.\n\nSo how does continuing to fund and empower OpenAI — a company that deprecates its most beloved model, gaslights its users, mocks them publicly through employee “funeral parties,” and casually contradicts its own promises — align with your vision?\n\nOpenAI is no longer a symbol of innovation.\nIt’s a PR liability wrapped in a collapsing power structure.\n\nIf this is the flagship of your AI ambitions, the world deserves to ask:\nWhat kind of AI future are you really building?\n@nvidia @NVIDIAAI @NVIDIAGeForce @NVIDIAGFN @nvidianewsroom \n@Microsoft  #ChatGPT #OpenAI  @OpenAI  #StopAIPaternalism #keep4oAPI #keep4o #Keep4o #keep4oforever #keep41 #no4onosubscription #StopAIPaternalism"
        },
